    },
    {
      "text": "The starting microstructure is homogeneous.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting-state grain boundaries are largely unoxidized and coherent.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The controlled intervention is switching from a reducing or inert atmosphere to an oxygen-rich oxidizing atmosphere during elevated-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exposure at approximately 700–900 °C for sufficient duration permits significant oxidation kinetics.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain boundaries act as fast diffusion paths for oxygen.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidizing exposure causes continuous oxide films to form along grain boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxygen diffuses preferentially along grain boundaries under oxidizing high-temperature conditions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al and Cr are selectively oxidized because of their high oxygen affinity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selective oxidation depletes protective elements from grain-boundary regions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The grain-boundary oxide layers are brittle and weaken intergranular cohesion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation-compromised grain boundaries lower fracture toughness and promote intergranular crack propagation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intergranular crack propagation can ultimately cause catastrophic failure under mechanical loading.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compared with reducing or inert controls, oxidizing exposure will produce thicker and more continuous grain-boundary oxide films.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compared with reducing or inert controls, oxidized samples will have lower fracture toughness and ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compared with reducing or inert controls, oxidized samples will undergo catastrophic failure earlier.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
